[
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"699016\">@Edison Xie</span> and I discovered an interesting issue:<br>\nIn <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/master/Mathlib/RingTheory/Valuation/ValuationRing.lean#L154\">RingTheory.Valuation.ValuationRing.lean L154</a>, if we remove the <code>set_option</code> before this def, this line fails. However appending a <code>with_reducible rfl</code> works. Does anyone have insight into what's going on here? Could this be a bug in <code>simp</code>?</p>\n<p>A lean 4 web version for this is <a href=\"https://live.lean-lang.org/#codez=JYWwDg9gTgLgBAWQIYwBYBtgCMBQOB2SIApgM5hIDGxcAakugK4rAT4BKw%2BA5ngG5IowJFnQ0AFAEE4ALjgAVAJ5gajAJRwA2gGEIIEJx5xJAXRwChIsXHEBpWQuU0%2BGzQDFgxdABM4tk1qS6NzEWFBIxn5mFsKiNJoAkqQAInpIXMYBmvRMLGyG3JlaSW7hlDCsHFyF0v54ALT1cKTEMAD6EGAVbHBYVADWAO6C3gB0wCnEAGYAogCOo1BkKuXy4fjkgsT4lIpwUwwtcFwEbJR6YIwwVjRcpNc7NFMQEA4AMlzEggDyUN7EUBsOUYxAA4lAIIwwJFbBpBqgAcQcHA4GI2kspuhZABeXp7IT4GAQuCAC%%2BN4OvgkS6Xdr9vvhUaTfm9CBmy7GVpAATCOBP3ZTklSCEIwiQUZQNNf4pgCFAAymN9CVQdEmQAJkAuAWTaE1ekQ%2BBAzff9NCA8QGEg8JkGhWo1FGEBD3vYgiOQt9iAADyoeASjKTMCnGfAACtiHKYBlzgNopJsT8hG4VB2gLR50EAAIIO2QhjbX0bND2PPYAEVGAgCpthgGDIXwbwAHJsy4njSQjUhRkYTcYB9dBgx5VkYBMhhBWBPIqh4UZeT8rFpLaZ1fOSMTgG8G43hmQVtHQQsBwLdBRn%2BSh2C8KSgA\">here</a>.</p>",
        "id": 617835721,
        "sender_full_name": "Jiang Jiedong",
        "timestamp": 1787284534
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>In the <code>hb : b = 0</code> branch the goal is essentially</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">@</span><span class=\"n\">Eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ValueGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Quot.mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">•</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Quot.mk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p><code>simp</code> has no trouble rewriting this down to <code>Quot.mk _ 0 = Quot.mk _ 0</code>, but then it can't close it with <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Init/SimpLemmas.html#eq_self\">eq_self</a>. To apply <code>eq_self : (a = a) = True</code> it has to assign the implicit <code>{α}</code> to <code>ValueGroup A K</code>, and then check that <code>Quot.mk _ 0</code> — whose type is <code>Quotient (MulAction.orbitRel Aˣ K)</code> — matches that. The two types are of course definitionally equal, but only at default transparency, whereas this check happens at implicit transparency. <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/RingTheory/Valuation/ValuationRing.html#ValuationRing.ValueGroup\">ValueGroup</a> is an ordinary <code>def</code> and hence semireducible, so it doesn't unfold there and the assignment fails.</p>\n<p>With <code>backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency</code> set to <code>false</code>, every semireducible definition is treated as implicit-reducible, so <code>ValueGroup</code> does unfold at that point and <code>simp</code> goes through.</p>\n<p>So I don't think \"bug\" is the right word here. I believe you could fix it by tagging <code>ValueGroup</code> with <code>@[implicit_reducible]</code>, but I'm not familiar with the math here, so I'm not sure whether that's a good idea.</p>",
        "id": 617843251,
        "sender_full_name": "Yongxi Lin (Aaron)",
        "timestamp": 1787288984
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Or, one could define the linear order via the Quotient linear order declaration. Or restructure the proof to not start with a rintro line, since that is what deconstructs in a way that breaks through API boundaries.</p>",
        "id": 617869533,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1787299951
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>If I do it via quotient induction, then you clearly get the error:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Note</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">The</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expression</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"n\">correct</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">under</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`implicit</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">transparency</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">level</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">may</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">triggered</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failure</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">This</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">usually</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">caused</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">unfolding</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">semireducible</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">definitions</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">prior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">steps</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`set_option</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">linter</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">tacticCheckInstances</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">true</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">investigate</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">source</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">issue</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span>\n<span class=\"n\">Full</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">error</span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">Application</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mismatch</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">The</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">argument</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"bp\">⟦</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">⟧</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">has</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Quotient</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">MulAction</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">orbitRel</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"bp\">ˣ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">but</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">type</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ValueGroup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">K</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">application</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">Eq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟦</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">⟧</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>When I start with</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">le_antisymm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">induction</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">using</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Quotient</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">inductionOn₂</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">rintro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">e</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">he</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hf</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Quotient</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">eq</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 617872041,
        "sender_full_name": "Yakov Pechersky",
        "timestamp": 1787300716
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have an example where simp does not close</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"bp\">**⊢**</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟦</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟦</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"bp\">⟧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- \\[[ ]] has not ambiguity</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>For whatever definition it is, I expect simp to close such goals.</p>",
